  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="24">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 24</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-g-a">And we lærað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man wið fúlne galscipe ⁊ wið unrihthæmed ⁊ wið æghwylcne æwbryce warnige symle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-a">And we lærað, þæt man wið fulne galscype ⁊ wið unrihthæmed ⁊ wið æghwylcne æwbrece wærnige symle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ we lærað, þæt man wiþ fulne galscipe ⁊ wið unrihthǽmed ⁊ wið æghwylce ǽwbryce warnian georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-q">Et ab inmundis gaudiis (a libidine) et iniusto concubitu uel adulterio caueatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="24" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ we lærað þæt man wið fulne galscipe ⁊ wið unrihthǽmed ⁊ wið æghwylce ǽwbryce warnian georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And we enjoin that foul lasciviousness and illicit unions and every [kind of] adultery be zealously abhorred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wir schreiben vor, dass man vor schmutziger Geilheit und vor gesetzwidrigem Beischlaf und vor jedem Ehebruch sich stets (ernstlich B) hüte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we instruct that people always (eagerly, B) beware of foul lust and unlawful intercourse and every kind of adultery.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G</note>
      </div>
    </body>
